── Thinking ────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
Now I have a clear picture. The InputRejected handler at line 977-991 records `FailureObserved` but does NOT record `ModelCallCompleted`. After InputRejected, the event loop continues (it doesn't break/return), so the channel might still deliver events or close. The channel-close cleanup at line 1092 would eventually catch it with `"stream_closed_without_agent_end"`, BUT only if the channel actually closes before the function returns. If yoagent holds the channel open expecting a retry, the `ModelCallStarted` from line 782 stays open.

The fix is straightforward: in the InputRejected handler, after recording FailureObserved, record ModelCallCompleted with status "input_rejected" and set `model_call_terminal_recorded = true`. This prevents the channel-close cleanup from double-recording and ensures every ModelCallStarted has a matching ModelCallCompleted.

